{"id": "EUVD-2026-59125", "enisaUuid": "a2f5c4e5-9697-3840-9861-4905dca0b28e", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nbatman-adv: tt: prevent TVLV OOB check overflow\n\nA TT unicast TVLV contains the number of VLANs stored in it. This number is\nan u16 and gets multiplied by the size of the struct\nbatadv_tvlv_tt_vlan_data (8 bytes). The size can therefore overflow the u16\nused to store the tt_vlan_len. All additional safety checks to prevent\nout-of-bounds access of the TVLV buffer are invalid due to this overflow.\n\nUsing size_t prevents this overflow and ensures that the safety checks\ncompare against the actual buffer requirements.", "datePublished": "2026-08-15T05:54:18", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-16T18:45:02", "baseScore": 9.8, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/0de12a4c4847f571d82a9cd96bc633eded41d7c6", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/d6ff4764ff784ede25f5c83a6f5883a74c93a5ea", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/1898273c5dc8148267ef9f97cd2517a2822350e7", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/604bd5042fbcd1ab9f7cd98fd847ec017aeede8a", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/7319c0794f91be2734aac695794e7203606b49f8", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/3256c05d5a9db34346eaf20f52dddde984852d77", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/6222b443686525cb5a9b6a9cecf23b2e2ab23e2a", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/7a581d9aaba8c82bd6177fa36b2588eea77f6e2b"], "aliases": ["GHSA-5r79-5r2g-4hhm", "CVE-2026-72226"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.76, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0d3ba758-c695-3bed-8551-647052ebaf75", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "7ea7b4a142758deaf46c1af0ca9ceca6dd55138b <3256c05d5a9db34346eaf20f52dddde984852d77"}, {"id": "155e11c6-9ff1-3a7a-a590-5e3500fa2c0e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.40"}, {"id": "1648f4dd-7512-3394